      },
      "message": "feat(post): Heidenhain DIN/ISO writes the G62 filter mode and checks the T range\n\nheidenhain.cps writes G62 T<tol> P01 <0 finish|1 rough> P02 0 where the\ncontrol profile takes P01. Two new resolver flags (g62_mode, g62_t_max_um)\ncarry the documented word and the largest T for each control and NC\nsoftware. A T above the range, a T that rounds to T0, and smoothing on a\ncontrol without cycle 32 are refused by name. The Picomax 55 (iTNC 530\n340490-03, option 2 not listed) keeps its G62 T-only output.\n\nFixes #4226\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
